  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Karnavati Sales Corporation vs Ahmedabad Municipal Corporation on 21 May, 2025 Author: Sanjay Kumar Bench: Sanjay Kumar 1 In The Supreme Court Of India Civil Appellate Jurisdiction Civil Appeal No. /2025",
    "facts": "Appellant No. 1, Karnavati Sales Corporation, is a sole proprietorship and its proprietor, namely, Kanaiyalal Pannalal, is stated to have expired on 21.01.2023. Appellant No. 2, Hajarbhai Surajmal Pannalal, is stated to have expired on 29.04.2021, while, Savarmal Sainee, the nominee of Kuber Tobacco Products Pvt. Ltd., appellant No. 3, expired on 30.04.2021. It is further stated that Kuber Tobacco Products Pvt. Ltd., which is shown independently as appellant No. 4, closed down in 2009 and surrendered its license under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Sanjay Kumar Pathak, learned counsel, appearing for the appellants, states that the present appeal does not survive for consideration on merits as the appellant Nos. 1, 3 and 4 are not in existence anymore and appellant No. 2, Hajarbhai Surajmal Pannalal, expired.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Sanjay Kumar Pathak, learned counsel, appearing for the appellants, states that the present appeal does not survive for consideration on merits as the appellant Nos. 1, 3 and 4 are not in existence anymore and appellant No. 2, Hajarbhai Surajmal Pannalal, expired.",
